            },
            "author": {
              "@type": "Person",
              "name": "Karen"
            },
            "reviewBody": "This came out pretty well, once I figured out the correct amount of milk to use (4 teaspoons, not 2). Otherwise, I made the recipe unchanged. My children are young, so don't relate the decorating ability to the quality of the recipe, ha.",
            "datePublished": "2023-12-25T03:37:05.792Z"
          },
          {
            "@type": "Review",
            "reviewRating": {
              "@type": "Rating",
              "ratingValue": "5"
            },
            "author": {
              "@type": "Person",
              "name": "JS"
            },
            "reviewBody": "Love! I skipped the corn syrup and instead made my own sugar syrup by boiling 1 1/4 C sugar and 3/4 C water, stirring until smooth and letting it cool while I made the rest.",
            "datePublished": "2018-12-10T01:10:52.597Z"
          },
          {
            "@type": "Review",
            "reviewRating": {
              "@type": "Rating",
              "ratingValue": "5"
            },
            "author": {
              "@type": "Person",
              "name": "Tammie"
            },
            "reviewBody": "Loved it, added almond extract and a Tablespoon of melted butter. Was a huge hit with everyone.",
            "datePublished": "2024-01-21T14:54:19.410Z"
          },
          {
            "@type": "Review",
            "reviewRating": {
              "@type": "Rating",
              "ratingValue": "5"
            },
            "author": {
              "@type": "Person",
              "name": "nicolekrystyn"
            },
            "reviewBody": "Perfect recipe! I grew up with almond extract in my birthday cake frosting so I love the almond extract flavor that adds a hint of extra sweetness and complexity. You can easily swap out for your extract of choice. I also have successfully used oat milk in this recipe since I was out of dairy milk. This icing is easy to thicken or thin depending on your preference and easy to double or triple as needed. Definitely my go-to recipe for sugar cookies!",
            "datePublished": "2022-12-27T16:30:17.503Z"
          },
          {
            "@type": "Review",
            "reviewRating": {
              "@type": "Rating",
              "ratingValue": "5"
            },
            "author": {
              "@type": "Person",
              "name": "Christina Martinez"
            },
            "reviewBody": "I have been searching for an easy yet tasty cookie icing recipe and I've found it! \nI added one more tspn of milk for the consistency I preferred and used both vanilla and lemon (a little goes a long way) extract instead of almond extract and it tastes amazing!! The icing gave that shiny, glossy look on the cookies and didn't take too long to harden. I will definitely be using this recipe from now on!",
            "datePublished": "2019-11-23T14:29:12.143Z"
          },
          {
            "@type": "Review",
            "reviewRating": {
              "@type": "Rating",
              "ratingValue": "5"
            },
            "author": {
              "@type": "Person",
              "name": "yasmins"
            },
            "reviewBody": "Very tasty! We added vanilla extract instead of almond. I also ended up using an extra teaspoon of milk because it was too stiff, and I felt the corn syrup was too thick. It doesn't make as much as I thought it would. We had barely enough to cover one large gingerbread man (about 5\" x 3\"). The icing dried very well.",
            "datePublished": "2019-12-19T15:50:48.880Z"
          },
